// =============================================================================
//  Solarized Dark — Telegram Desktop palette
//
//  Apply via:  Telegram → Settings → Chat Settings → Choose from file → pick
//              this .tdesktop-palette.  Telegram saves the result as the
//              active theme; switching back is one click on any theme tile.
//
//  Built on top of the default "night" base — only the keys that drive the
//  overall feel are overridden, and Telegram fills the rest with sensible
//  Solarized-compatible defaults from the night palette.  This keeps the
//  file short and survives Telegram updates that add new colour keys.
//
//  Palette reference (Ethan Schoonover, https://ethanschoonover.com/solarized):
//      base03  #002b36   (deepest bg)
//      base02  #073642   (panel bg)
//      base01  #586e75   (muted fg)
//      base00  #657b83   (body fg alt)
//      base0   #839496   (body fg)
//      base1   #93a1a1   (emphasised fg)
//      base2   #eee8d5   (light bg)
//      base3   #fdf6e3   (lightest bg)
//      yellow  #b58900   orange #cb4b16   red    #dc322f
//      magenta #d33682   violet #6c71c4   blue   #268bd2
//      cyan    #2aa198   green  #859900
// =============================================================================

